1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,100
Before it calculates, Modori asks. When the evidence is not enough, it abstains.

2
00:00:07,100 --> 00:00:15,133
Here is the payoff: a reviewable result from 649 public student records, exported to Word locally.

3
00:00:15,133 --> 00:00:23,033
I'm a social-science student. I built Modori because starting statistical work should feel clear, not punishing.

4
00:00:23,033 --> 00:00:33,333
This walkthrough uses 649 observed records from UCI Student Performance. Modori labels the 30-row preview before loading the full table.

5
00:00:33,333 --> 00:00:43,967
Before any method appears, I confirm what the variables mean: study time is ordinal; final grade is scale. These decisions enter the review trail.

6
00:00:43,967 --> 00:00:56,767
I ask whether study time and grades move together, then assign exact roles. Modori asks bounded questions about independence, clustering, and weights, and records the answers.

7
00:00:56,767 --> 00:01:07,267
The reviewable candidate is Spearman correlation. Its association-only boundary, variables, missing-data policy, and experimental status remain visible.

8
00:01:07,267 --> 00:01:19,267
Prepare seals the reviewed configuration but does not calculate. Only this separate Run action produces the result: rho point two seven five, p below point zero zero one.

9
00:01:19,267 --> 00:01:29,633
A second request asks for a causal effect. Modori does not substitute a convenient method. It records that the request is outside the current scope.

10
00:01:29,633 --> 00:01:47,067
During Build Week, Codex with GPT-5.6 helped turn product questions into contracts, failing tests, implementation, and Windows verification, from variable meaning and ledger authority to Excel recovery, safe Word export, and failure recovery.

11
00:01:47,067 --> 00:01:58,467
The arithmetic and recommendation boundary are tested separately. External reference checks support the calculation layer, while the workflow remains reviewable from data to report.

12
00:01:58,467 --> 00:02:05,033
Modori asks, abstains, and waits for you to Run. Kindness is a system behavior.
